# ==============================================================================
# AquariusOS — the apps that come with the OS
# ==============================================================================
# Plain English: this file is the SHOPPING LIST. It does not install anything by
# itself. It just says "these apps are part of AquariusOS", and the small
# service aquarius-flatpak-preinstall.service does the actual downloading the
# first time the machine has internet.
#
# WHAT IS ON THIS LIST, AND WHAT IS NOT (decided by Royce, 2026-08-28)
#
# Only a web browser is unconditional. Everything a creator might want — OBS,
# Audacity, Blender, DaVinci Resolve — is OFFERED instead, in a single tick-box
# window on the first login, with everything pre-ticked. The reasoning: a
# browser is the one app a computer is unusable without, so it should simply be
# there; a 3 GB 3D suite should be a choice somebody made, even if making it
# takes one click. See /usr/libexec/aquarius-creator-apps-offer.
#
# Two browsers rather than one, because people arrive with an existing habit and
# the machine should not argue with it.
#
# The file format is Flatpak's own, documented in `man flatpak-preinstall`. Each
# app gets a block whose heading is its full Flathub app ID.
#
# Two things worth knowing:
#
#   * Branch=stable is NOT optional. If you leave it out, Flatpak looks for a
#     branch called "master", which Flathub apps do not have, and the install
#     quietly finds nothing.
#
#   * The user always wins. If somebody uninstalls one of these, it stays
#     uninstalled — Flatpak remembers the removal and does not put it back.
#     That is deliberate and matches how the rest of AquariusOS behaves.
#
# TO ADD AN APP: copy a block, change the ID to the one shown on the app's
# flathub.org page, keep Branch=stable. Check the ID really exists first —
# https://flathub.org/apps/<the-id> should load. A typo here is silent.
#
# ⚠️ Before adding anything, ask whether it belongs in the first-login OFFER
# instead. This list is for things that should be on every AquariusOS machine
# whether the owner asked or not, and that is a very short list.
#
# The beginner write-up: docs/creator-apps.md
# ==============================================================================

# ---- Browsers ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Firefox. Note for anyone comparing us to stock Bazzite: Bazzite does ship
# Firefox, but it installs it from the LIVE USB during installation, and the
# AquariusOS installer deliberately does not do that (installer/build.sh). So on
# AquariusOS this line is what actually puts Firefox on the machine — it is not
# a duplicate. On a machine that came from Bazzite and was switched over to us,
# Firefox is already there and Flatpak simply leaves it alone.
#
# Installing it system-wide also matters on the NVIDIA edition: Bazzite's own
# start-up housekeeping sets Firefox's hardware-video-decode settings with
# `flatpak override --system`, and those only reach a system-installed Firefox.
[Flatpak Preinstall org.mozilla.firefox]
Branch=stable

# Google Chrome. This one is unusual: Flathub is not allowed to redistribute
# Chrome, so the Flatpak is a small wrapper that downloads Google's own
# installer from google.com at install time ("extra-data"). Consequences:
#   * it needs internet at install time (so does everything else here), and
#   * very occasionally Google removes an old build before Flathub catches up,
#     and this one app fails to install. The service handles that: it installs
#     everything it can and tries the stragglers again on the next boot.
[Flatpak Preinstall com.google.Chrome]
Branch=stable
